    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for expat.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 10.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "Expat is a C library for parsing XML documents.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* expat: Expat: Denial of Service via quadratic complexity in attribute processing (CVE-2026-66046)\n\n* expat: Expat: XML Injection via Malformed UTF-16 Input (CVE-2026-93990)\n\n* expat: expat: Denial of Service via integer overflow in expat_realloc (CVE-2026-102633)\n\n* expat: expat: Information disclosure via heap buffer over-read in XML_ParseBuffer (CVE-2026-77214)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
        "category": "legal_disclaimer",
        "text": "This content is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). If you distribute this content, or a modified version of it, you must provide attribution to the original copyright holder(s) and provide a link to the original.",
